<header><h1>The Mentak Coalition: Proof</h1></header>
<article>
<p>The source text behind each note on <a href="/F_mentak">The Mentak Coalition</a>. <b>Explicit</b> sources state the note directly. <b>Implicit</b> sources support it without stating it.</p>

<h2 id="ambush"><a href="https://twilight-imperium.fandom.com/wiki/The_Mentak_Coalition#Faction_Abilities:~:text=Ambush">Ambush</a></h2>
    <ol class="note">
    <li>Game effects that reroll, modify, or otherwise affect combat rolls do not affect dice rolls made when resolving the <sc>Ambush</sc> ability.<sup>2</sup>
        <ul>
        <li><b>Explicit</b>: <sup>2</sup> RulesPal, &ldquo;How does Mentak&rsquo;s Ambush work?&rdquo;: &ldquo;It isn&rsquo;t a combat roll, so Morale Boost doesn&rsquo;t apply.&rdquo;</li>
        </ul></li>
    <li>If a cruiser or destroyer is removed before the Mentak player can resolve their <sc>Ambush</sc> ability, that ship cannot be one of the ships used when they do resolve their <sc>Ambush</sc> ability.<sup>2</sup>
        <ul>
        <li><b>Implicit</b>: <sup>2</sup> Same entry: &ldquo;roll one die for each of up to 2 cruisers or destroyers.&rdquo; A removed ship cannot roll.</li>
        </ul></li>
    <li>The <a href="https://twilight-imperium.fandom.com/wiki/Action_Cards#Twilight_Imperium_Fourth_Edition:~:text=Shields%20Holding"><i>Shields Holding</i></a> action card may be used to cancel the hit.<sup>1,2</sup>
        <ul>
        <li><b>Explicit</b>: <sup>1</sup> LRR FAQ: &ldquo;&rsquo;Shields Holding&rsquo; may be used to cancel hits that are produced by these abilities,&rdquo; including &ldquo;Ambush.&rdquo;</li>
        <li><b>Implicit</b>: <sup>2</sup> RulesPal, &ldquo;Do Direct Hit and Shields Holding work on hits from Dimensional Splicer or Yin Devotion?&rdquo;: &ldquo;Yes to both.&rdquo;</li>
        </ul></li>
    <li>A ship may cancel the hit by using its <a href="/R_sustain_damage"><sc>Sustain Damage</sc></a> ability, if present.<sup>1</sup>
        <ul>
        <li><b>Explicit</b>: <sup>1</sup> LRR 87.4: a unit &ldquo;can use its &lsquo;Sustain Damage&rsquo; ability any time a hit is produced against it.&rdquo;</li>
        </ul></li>
    <ol><li>If the chosen ship does so, the <a href="https://twilight-imperium.fandom.com/wiki/Action_Cards#Twilight_Imperium_Fourth_Edition:~:text=Direct%20Hit"><i>Direct Hit</i></a> action card may be played.<sup>1</sup>
        <ul>
        <li><b>Explicit</b>: <sup>1</sup> LRR FAQ: &ldquo;&rsquo;Direct Hit&rsquo; can be used to follow up hits that are assigned by &lsquo;Ambush,&rsquo; &lsquo;Dimensional Splicer,&rsquo; &lsquo;Devotion,&rsquo; and other similar abilities.&rdquo;</li>
        </ul></li></ol>
    <li>Ships that roll dice for <sc>Ambush</sc> still make combat rolls as normal, starting in the first round of combat.<sup>2</sup>
        <ul>
        <li><b>Explicit</b>: <sup>2</sup> RulesPal, &ldquo;How does Mentak&rsquo;s Ambush work?&rdquo;: &ldquo;the ambushing ships still roll normally from the first round.&rdquo;</li>
        </ul></li>
    </ol>

<h2 id="pillage"><a href="https://twilight-imperium.fandom.com/wiki/The_Mentak_Coalition#Faction_Abilities:~:text=Pillage">Pillage</a></h2>
    <ol class="note">
    <li>While the agenda phase allows a player to resolve transactions with all other players, it does not make that player neighbors with the Mentak player.<sup>2,5</sup>
        <ul>
        <li><b>Explicit</b>: <sup>2</sup> RulesPal, &ldquo;How often can the Mentak use Pillage, and does it work in the agenda phase against everyone?&rdquo;: &ldquo;the agenda phase does not make everyone neighbors: transactions with non-neighbors are allowed then, yet Pillage still only works on the Mentak&rsquo;s actual neighbors, as the developer ruled.&rdquo;</li>
        <li><b>Explicit</b>: <sup>5</sup> Designer ruling (x3n d0g, 01/17/2019): &ldquo;Simply being in the agenda phase does not confer neighbor status to all players.&rdquo;</li>
        </ul></li>
    <li>If the <a href="/F_creuss">Creuss</a> player has units or controls planets in a system with an alpha wormhole, and the Mentak player has units or controls planets in a system with a beta wormhole, or vice versa, then the <a href="/F_creuss">Creuss</a> player and Mentak player are neighbors. The Mentak player may thus use their <sc>Pillage</sc> ability against the <a href="/F_creuss">Creuss</a> player.<sup>1</sup>
        <ul>
        <li><b>Explicit</b>: <sup>1</sup> LRR FAQ: Mentak may use Pillage when &ldquo;neighbors with another faction as a result of the &hellip; &lsquo;Quantum Entanglement&rsquo; faction ability &hellip; because the &lsquo;neighbor&rsquo; status is active as a result of the ability.&rdquo;</li>
        </ul></li>
    <li>If the <a href="/F_winnu">Winnu</a> player owns <a href="https://twilight-imperium.fandom.com/wiki/The_Winnu#Faction_Technologies:~:text=Lazax%20Gate%20Folding"><i>Lazax Gate Folding</i></a>, then the Mentak player may become neighbors with the <a href="/F_winnu">Winnu</a> player during the <a href="/F_winnu">Winnu</a> player&rsquo;s tactical action. If so, the Mentak player may use their <sc>Pillage</sc> ability during this time.<sup>1,5</sup>
        <ul>
        <li><b>Explicit</b>: <sup>1</sup> LRR FAQ: Mentak may use Pillage &ldquo;when they are neighbors with another faction as a result of the &lsquo;Lazax Gate Folding&rsquo; faction technology.&rdquo;</li>
        <li><b>Explicit</b>: <sup>5</sup> Designer ruling (Vinci, 12/11/2018): &ldquo;rules as written, the Mentak would be able to pillage the transaction.&rdquo;</li>
        </ul></li>
    <li>The Mentak player may use their <sc>Pillage</sc> ability even if the transaction does not involve trade goods.<sup>2</sup>
        <ul>
        <li><b>Explicit</b>: <sup>2</sup> RulesPal, &ldquo;When exactly can Mentak use Pillage?&rdquo;: &ldquo;After each instance of a neighbor gaining trade goods or resolving a transaction.&rdquo;</li>
        </ul></li>
    <li>The Mentak player may use their <sc>Pillage</sc> ability against both players involved in a transaction.<sup>2,5</sup>
        <ul>
        <li><b>Explicit</b>: <sup>2</sup> RulesPal, &ldquo;When exactly can Mentak use Pillage?&rdquo;: &ldquo;Both sides of a transaction between two neighbors can each be pillaged, in the order Mentak chooses.&rdquo;</li>
        <li><b>Explicit</b>: <sup>5</sup> Designer ruling (sigmazero13, Aug 15, 2018): &ldquo;so yes, you would be able to steal from both.&rdquo;</li>
        </ul></li>
    <li>If the Mentak player resolves a transaction with another player, they may then use their <sc>Pillage</sc> ability against that player.<sup>2</sup>
        <ul>
        <li><b>Explicit</b>: <sup>2</sup> RulesPal, &ldquo;When exactly can Mentak use Pillage?&rdquo;: &ldquo;After each instance of a neighbor &hellip; resolving a transaction.&rdquo;</li>
        </ul></li>
    <ol><li>The Mentak player does not decide to use their <sc>Pillage</sc> ability until after the transaction has been resolved. Any deal made to not use their <sc>Pillage</sc> ability before the transaction has been resolved is non&ndash;binding.<sup>*</sup>
        <ul>
        <li><b>Unverified</b>: No source found.</li>
        </ul></li></ol>
    <li>Effects that force players to give objects to other players are not transactions.<sup>*</sup>
        <ul>
        <li><b>Unverified</b>: No source found.</li>
        </ul></li>
    <ol><li>If Alice plays Bob&rsquo;s <a href="https://twilight-imperium.fandom.com/wiki/Promissory_Notes#Trade_Agreement"><i>Trade Agreement</i></a> promissory note, then the Mentak player may use <sc>Pillage</sc> on Alice, but not Bob.<sup>*</sup>
        <ul>
        <li><b>Unverified</b>: No source found.</li>
        </ul></li></ol>
    <li>If a player would gain multiple trade goods one at a time, the Mentak player can use their <sc>Pillage</sc> ability for each trade good.<sup>2,5</sup>
        <ul>
        <li><b>Explicit</b>: <sup>2</sup> RulesPal, &ldquo;How often can the Mentak use Pillage, and does it work in the agenda phase against everyone?&rdquo;: &ldquo;Pillage triggers separately each time a neighbor gains trade goods or resolves a transaction.&rdquo;</li>
        <li><b>Implicit</b>: <sup>5</sup> Designer ruling (sigmazero13, Aug 15, 2018): &ldquo;This ability triggers for each instance of a neighbor gaining trade goods or resolving a transaction&rdquo; Pillage triggers per instance of gaining.</li>
        </ul></li>
    <li>The Mentak player may use their <sc>Pillage</sc> ability each time the <a href="/F_saar">Saar</a> player gains a trade good from their <a href="https://twilight-imperium.fandom.com/wiki/The_Clan_of_Saar#Faction_Abilities:~:text=Scavenge"><sc>Scavenge</sc></a> faction ability during a single turn, if all of the conditions of <sc>Pillage</sc> are met.<sup>1</sup>
        <ul>
        <li><b>Explicit</b>: <sup>1</sup> LRR FAQ: &ldquo;Can the Mentak Coalition use the &lsquo;Pillage&rsquo; faction ability for each time the Saar gain a trade good from the &lsquo;Scavenge&rsquo; faction ability in a single turn &hellip;? A: Yes.&rdquo;</li>
        </ul></li>
    <li>If a game effect instructs a player to convert their commodities to trade goods, that player does not gain any trade goods from that effect. The Mentak player cannot use their <sc>Pillage</sc> ability for those trade goods.<sup>4</sup>
        <ul>
        <li><b>Explicit</b>: <sup>4</sup> Designer ruling: &ldquo;whenever commodities are converted to a player&rsquo;s own trade good area, they are not considered gained.&rdquo;</li>
        </ul></li>
    <li>A player cannot spend trade goods after the conditions of <sc>Pillage</sc> are met and before the Mentak player resolves it.<sup>2</sup>
        <ul>
        <li><b>Explicit</b>: <sup>2</sup> RulesPal, &ldquo;When exactly can Mentak use Pillage?&rdquo;: &ldquo;Nobody can dump trade goods between the trigger and Pillage.&rdquo;</li>
        </ul></li>
    </ol>

<h2 id="promise-of-protection"><a href="https://twilight-imperium.fandom.com/wiki/The_Mentak_Coalition#Faction_Promissory_Note:~:text=Promise%20of%20Protection">Promise of Protection</a> <sub>(Promissory Note)</sub></h2>
    <ol class="note">
    <li>If the player with <i>Promise of Protection</i> in their play area resolves a transaction with another player, the Mentak player may still use their <a href="https://twilight-imperium.fandom.com/wiki/The_Mentak_Coalition#Faction_Abilities:~:text=Pillage"><sc>Pillage</sc></a> ability on that other player.<sup>2</sup>
        <ul>
        <li><b>Implicit</b>: <sup>2</sup> RulesPal: Pillage needs a neighbor with &ldquo;no face-up Promise of Protection.&rdquo; The protection belongs only to the holder.</li>
        </ul></li>
    <li><i>Promise of Protection</i> has no effect while it is in a player&rsquo;s hand.<sup>2</sup>
        <ul>
        <li><b>Explicit</b>: <sup>2</sup> RulesPal, &ldquo;If I hold Mentak&rsquo;s Promise of Protection without playing it &hellip;?&rdquo;: &ldquo;it also doesn&rsquo;t protect you from Pillage until it is face up in your play area.&rdquo;</li>
        </ul></li>
    <li><i>Promise of Protection</i> is returned when the system is activated, even if the active player will perform no hostile acts toward the Mentak player this turn.<sup>*</sup>
        <ul>
        <li><b>Unverified</b>: No source found.</li>
        </ul></li>
    <li>Activating a system containing only the Mentak player&rsquo;s structures will still cause <i>Promise of Protection</i> to be returned.<sup>*</sup>
        <ul>
        <li><b>Unverified</b>: No source found.</li>
        </ul></li>
    <li>If an effect other than activating a system during a tactical action places a command token in a system with the Mentak player&rsquo;s units (for example, the primary ability of the <a href="/R_diplomacy"><i>Diplomacy</i></a> strategy card), this will not cause <i>Promise of Protection</i> to be returned.<sup>*</sup>
        <ul>
        <li><b>Unverified</b>: No source found.</li>
        </ul></li>
    </ol>

<h2 id="mirror-computing"><a href="https://twilight-imperium.fandom.com/wiki/The_Mentak_Coalition#Faction_Technologies:~:text=Mirror%20Computing">Mirror Computing</a> <sub>(Technology)</sub></h2>
    <ol class="note">
    <li>If an effect specifically requires that trade goods are spent (for example, the <a href="https://twilight-imperium.fandom.com/wiki/Objectives#Twilight_Imperium_Fourth_Edition:~:text=Negotiate%20Trade%20Routes"><i>Negotiate Trade Routes</i></a> objective), <i>Mirror Computing</i> does not increase the value of those trade goods.<sup>2</sup>
        <ul>
        <li><b>Explicit</b>: <sup>2</sup> RulesPal, &ldquo;How does Mentak&rsquo;s Mirror Computing interact with Bribery or spend-trade-goods objectives?&rdquo;: &ldquo;still 1 when spent as trade goods, so Bribery and objectives that spend trade goods get no bonus.&rdquo;</li>
        </ul></li>
    </ol>

<h2 id="salvage-operations"><a href="https://twilight-imperium.fandom.com/wiki/The_Mentak_Coalition#Faction_Technologies:~:text=Salvage%20Operations">Salvage Operations</a> <sub>(Technology)</sub></h2>
    <ol class="note">
    <li>If the space combat ends in a draw, <i>Salvage Operations</i> has no effect.<sup>5</sup>
        <ul>
        <li><b>Explicit</b>: <sup>5</sup> Designer ruling (Skootur, 1/25/2019): &ldquo;A draw is neither a win nor a loss. In both cases, Salvage Operations is not triggered.&rdquo;</li>
        </ul></li>
    <li>If the opponent has a faction specific ship, including their flagship, destroyed, the Mentak player may use their <i>Salvage Operations</i> to produce a generic ship of the same type, or their <a href="https://twilight-imperium.fandom.com/wiki/The_Mentak_Coalition#Flagship:~:text=Fourth%20Moon"><i>Fourth Moon</i></a>, as appropriate.<sup>1</sup>
        <ul>
        <li><b>Explicit</b>: <sup>1</sup> LRR FAQ: &ldquo;Can the Mentak Coalition use the &lsquo;Salvage Operations&rsquo; &hellip; to produce their own flagship after destroying an opponent&rsquo;s flagship? A: Yes, even though the units are technically different, they share the flagship unit type.&rdquo;</li>
        </ul></li>
    <li>The Mentak player cannot produce ground forces using <i>Salvage Operations</i>, even if their opponent has the ability to treat a ground force as a ship.<sup>1</sup>
        <ul>
        <li><b>Explicit</b>: <sup>1</sup> LRR FAQ: &ldquo;Can the Mentak Coalition use the &lsquo;Salvage Operations&rsquo; &hellip; to produce infantry after a combat against &hellip; &lsquo;The Alastor&rsquo; &hellip;? A: No, the infantry do not count as ships once the combat is over.&rdquo;</li>
        </ul></li>
    <li>The Mentak player cannot produce a war sun unless they have their war sun technology.<sup>1,2,3,5</sup>
        <ul>
        <li><b>Explicit</b>: <sup>1</sup> LRR FAQ: &ldquo;Without war sun technology, they cannot produce a war sun, even using &lsquo;Salvage Operations.&rsquo;&rdquo;</li>
        <li><b>Explicit</b>: <sup>3</sup> Learn to Play, war sun: &ldquo;You cannot produce this unit unless you own its unit upgrade technology.&rdquo;</li>
        <li><b>Explicit</b>: <sup>5</sup> Designer ruling: &ldquo;the Mentak player cannot use Salvage Operations to produce a War Sun if he does not have War Sun technology.&rdquo;</li>
        <li><b>Implicit</b>: <sup>2</sup> RulesPal, on the Vuil&rsquo;raith: &ldquo;by analogy with rulings on Mentak&rsquo;s Salvage Operations.&rdquo;</li>
        </ul></li>
    <li>The produced unit must be paid for.<sup>1,2</sup>
        <ul>
        <li><b>Explicit</b>: <sup>1</sup> LRR FAQ: &ldquo;a unit that is produced must always be paid for.&rdquo;</li>
        <li><b>Implicit</b>: <sup>2</sup> RulesPal, &ldquo;How does Saar&rsquo;s Chaos Mapping production work?&rdquo;: &ldquo;you still pay for it.&rdquo;</li>
        </ul></li>
    <li>If the Mentak player wishes to place a unit using their <i>Salvage Operations</i> ability, but there are none of that type left in their reinforcements, they can remove a unit of that type from any system that does not contain one of their command tokens and place that instead.<sup>1,3</sup>
        <ul>
        <li><b>Explicit</b>: <sup>1</sup> LRR 23.4a: &ldquo;that player can remove a unit from any system that does not contain one of their command tokens and place that unit in their reinforcements.&rdquo;</li>
        <li><b>Explicit</b>: <sup>3</sup> Learn to Play: &ldquo;When a player wishes to produce a unit but has no units of that type available in their reinforcements, that player may remove one of their units of that type from a system that does not contain one of their command tokens.&rdquo;</li>
        </ul></li>
    </ol>

<h2 id="fourth-moon"><a href="https://twilight-imperium.fandom.com/wiki/The_Mentak_Coalition#Flagship:~:text=Fourth%20Moon">Fourth Moon</a> <sub>(Flagship)</sub></h2>
    <ol class="note">
    <li>The <i>Fourth Moon</i> prevents other players&rsquo; ships from using <a href="/R_sustain_damage"><sc>Sustain Damage</sc></a> during a combat round in which it is destroyed, as <a href="/R_sustain_damage"><sc>Sustain Damage</sc></a> is used before the <i>Fourth Moon</i> is removed.<sup>2</sup>
        <ul>
        <li><b>Explicit</b>: <sup>2</sup> RulesPal, &ldquo;Do Mentak ships that Ambush still roll in the first round, and how does The Fourth Moon block Sustain Damage?&rdquo;: &ldquo;The Fourth Moon stops other players&rsquo; Sustain Damage in any round it takes part in, including the round it is destroyed, because Sustain Damage is used before hits remove it.&rdquo;</li>
        </ul></li>
    </ol>

<h2 id="suffi-an"><a href="https://twilight-imperium.fandom.com/wiki/The_Mentak_Coalition#Leaders:~:text=Suffi%20An">Suffi An</a> <sub>(Agent)</sub></h2>
    <ol class="note">
    </ol>

<h2 id="sula-mentarion"><a href="https://twilight-imperium.fandom.com/wiki/The_Mentak_Coalition#Leaders:~:text=S%27ula%20Mentarion">S&rsquo;ula Mentarion</a> <sub>(Commander)</sub></h2>
    <ol class="note">
    <li>The Mentak player&rsquo;s opponent chooses which promissory note they give to the Mentak player.<sup>2</sup>
        <ul>
        <li><b>Explicit</b>: <sup>2</sup> RulesPal, &ldquo;With Diplomatic Pressure or the Mentak commander, who picks the promissory note handed over?&rdquo;: &ldquo;The target does.&rdquo;</li>
        </ul></li>
    <li>Giving a promissory note because of S&rsquo;ula Mentarion is not resolving a transaction.<sup>*</sup>
        <ul>
        <li><b>Unverified</b>: No source found.</li>
        </ul></li>
    <li>If the Mentak player resolves their <a href="https://twilight-imperium.fandom.com/wiki/The_Mentak_Coalition#Faction_Technologies:~:text=Salvage%20Operations"><i>Salvage Operations</i></a> to place their fourth cruiser faction technology after winning a space combat, they cannot use the ability of S&rsquo;ula Mentarion from winning that combat.<sup>*</sup>
        <ul>
        <li><b>Unverified</b>: No source found.</li>
        </ul></li>
    <li>If the Mentak player places their fourth cruiser during combat, such as by the effect of <a href="https://twilight-imperium.fandom.com/wiki/The_Mentak_Coalition#Leaders:~:text=Sleeper%20Cell"><i>Sleeper Cell</i></a>, they may unlock and use the ability of S&rsquo;ula Mentarion at the end of that combat, should they win.<sup>*</sup>
        <ul>
        <li><b>Unverified</b>: No source found.</li>
        </ul></li>
    <ol><li>The four cruisers need not survive until the end of combat; S&rsquo;ula Mentarion is unlocked from the placement of the fourth cruiser on the game board.<sup>*</sup>
        <ul>
        <li><b>Unverified</b>: No source found.</li>
        </ul></li></ol>
    </ol>

<h2 id="ipswitch-loose-cannon"><a href="https://twilight-imperium.fandom.com/wiki/The_Mentak_Coalition#Leaders:~:text=Ipswitch%2C%20Loose%20Cannon">Ipswitch, Loose Cannon</a> &mdash; <a href="https://twilight-imperium.fandom.com/wiki/The_Mentak_Coalition#Leaders:~:text=Sleeper%20Cell">Sleeper Cell</a> <sub>(Hero)</sub></h2>
    <ol class="note">
    <li>The Mentak player can trigger the <i>Sleeper Cell</i> ability, their <a href="https://twilight-imperium.fandom.com/wiki/The_Mentak_Coalition#Faction_Abilities:~:text=Ambush"><sc>Ambush</sc></a> ability, or any other &ldquo;at the start of a space combat&rdquo; abilities they have in any order.<sup>*</sup>
        <ul>
        <li><b>Unverified</b>: No source found.</li>
        </ul></li>
    <li>If ships are destroyed before the <i>Sleeper Cell</i> ability is triggered, the Mentak player cannot place those units.<sup>*</sup>
        <ul>
        <li><b>Unverified</b>: No source found.</li>
        </ul></li>
    <li>Capacity is not checked during combat. As such, the Mentak player may place an unlimited number of fighters into a combat with this ability.<sup>3</sup>
        <ul>
        <li><b>Implicit</b>: <sup>3</sup> Learn to Play: &ldquo;During combat, a player&rsquo;s fighters and ground forces can exceed their ships&rsquo; capacity, but at the end of the combat, any excess units are destroyed.&rdquo; Capacity is not enforced mid-combat.</li>
        </ul></li>
    <li>Unlike capacity, the fleet pool limit applies at all times, including during combat. If placing ships with this ability causes the number of the Mentak player&rsquo;s non-fighter ships in the active system to exceed the number of command tokens in their fleet pool, they must immediately remove the excess ships, returning them to their reinforcements.<sup>1,2</sup>
        <ul>
        <li><b>Explicit</b>: <sup>1</sup> LRR 37.3: &ldquo;If at any time the number of a player&rsquo;s non-fighter ships in a system exceeds the number of tokens in that player&rsquo;s fleet pool, they choose and remove excess ships in that system, returning those units to their reinforcements.&rdquo;</li>
        <li><b>Explicit</b>: <sup>2</sup> RulesPal, &ldquo;When is the fleet pool limit checked, and can I bring extra ships into a fight and trim afterwards?&rdquo;: &ldquo;At all times, except for ships that are only moving through other systems.&rdquo;</li>
        </ul></li>
    <li>If all of the Mentak player&rsquo;s ships are destroyed, they may still place ships with this ability. If they do, combat will continue.<sup>2,4</sup>
        <ul>
        <li><b>Explicit</b>: <sup>4</sup> Designer ruling: &ldquo;If Mentak&rsquo;s Hero, Sleeper Cell, is used and their last ship is destroyed during a round of combat in which they also destroy an opponent&rsquo;s ship, does combat continue? A: Yes.&rdquo;</li>
        <li><b>Explicit</b>: <sup>2</sup> RulesPal, &ldquo;How does the Mentak hero work, and can it be escaped?&rdquo;: &ldquo;the combat can continue even if your other ships died.&rdquo;</li>
        </ul></li>
    <li>No costs are paid for the placed units.<sup>*</sup>
        <ul>
        <li><b>Unverified</b>: No source found.</li>
        </ul></li>
    <li>Both players will choose and destroy one of their own ships in the active system for each hit their opponent produced during each round of combat, before the Mentak player places their ships for the <i>Sleeper Cell</i> ability.<sup>4</sup>
        <ul>
        <li><b>Explicit</b>: <sup>4</sup> Designer ruling: &ldquo;after both players assign hits the Mentak player then places a ship from their reinforcements in the active system and combat continues.&rdquo;</li>
        </ul></li>
    <ol><li>When players would use their ships&rsquo; <a href="/R_sustain_damage"><sc>Sustain Damage</sc></a> abilities, they do so in alternating order, starting with the attacker. If the Mentak player uses a <a href="https://twilight-imperium.fandom.com/wiki/Action_Cards#Twilight_Imperium_Fourth_Edition:~:text=Direct%20Hit"><i>Direct Hit</i></a> action card to destroy one of their opponent&rsquo;s ships, they must then make the choice immediately if they will replace it using the <i>Sleeper Cell</i> ability, before any other ships may use their <a href="/R_sustain_damage"><sc>Sustain Damage</sc></a> ability. Should the Mentak version of the newly placed ship type have a <a href="/R_sustain_damage"><sc>Sustain Damage</sc></a> ability, it may then use it during the same combat round.<sup>*</sup>
        <ul>
        <li><b>Unverified</b>: No source found.</li>
        </ul></li></ol>
    <li>If the Mentak player wishes to place a unit with this ability, but there are none of that type left in their reinforcements, they may remove a unit of that type from any system that does not contain one of their command tokens and place that instead. This unit will be placed undamaged.<sup>1,4</sup>
        <ul>
        <li><b>Explicit</b>: <sup>1</sup> LRR 23.4a: &ldquo;that player can remove a unit from any system that does not contain one of their command tokens and place that unit in their reinforcements.&rdquo;</li>
        <li><b>Explicit</b>: <sup>4</sup> Designer ruling: &ldquo;If a unit is damaged, and is &lsquo;removed and placed&rsquo; from the board via a game effect, does it come back repaired &hellip;? A: &hellip; If it is produced, placed, or replaced which would require a remove and place it is no longer damaged.&rdquo;</li>
        </ul></li>
    <li>If the <a href="https://twilight-imperium.fandom.com/wiki/The_Mentak_Coalition#Flagship:~:text=Fourth%20Moon"><i>Fourth Moon</i></a> is destroyed during combat, but the Mentak player then destroys their opponent&rsquo;s flagship and places the <a href="https://twilight-imperium.fandom.com/wiki/The_Mentak_Coalition#Flagship:~:text=Fourth%20Moon"><i>Fourth Moon</i></a> back into the combat, they cannot score the <a href="https://twilight-imperium.fandom.com/wiki/Objectives#Twilight_Imperium_Fourth_Edition_3:~:text=Unveil%20Flagship"><i>Unveil Flagship</i></a> objective.<sup>4</sup>
        <ul>
        <li><b>Explicit</b>: <sup>4</sup> Designer ruling: &ldquo;If you use the Mentak Coalition&rsquo;s Hero &hellip; and lose your flagship in a combat, but destroy the other player&rsquo;s flagship and rebuild your own, can you score Unveil Flagship? A: No.&rdquo;</li>
        </ul></li>
    <ol><li>If the Mentak player starts the combat without the <a href="https://twilight-imperium.fandom.com/wiki/The_Mentak_Coalition#Flagship:~:text=Fourth%20Moon"><i>Fourth Moon</i></a>, and places it during the combat, they may score the <a href="https://twilight-imperium.fandom.com/wiki/Objectives#Twilight_Imperium_Fourth_Edition_3:~:text=Unveil%20Flagship"><i>Unveil Flagship</i></a> objective if the <a href="https://twilight-imperium.fandom.com/wiki/The_Mentak_Coalition#Flagship:~:text=Fourth%20Moon"><i>Fourth Moon</i></a> is not destroyed.<sup>*</sup>
        <ul>
        <li><b>Unverified</b>: No source found.</li>
        </ul></li></ol>
    <li>If a destroyed unit is a ground force or structure, that the other player is treating as a ship due to some effect, the Mentak player cannot place that unit.<sup>*</sup>
        <ul>
        <li><b>Unverified</b>: No source found.</li>
        </ul></li>
    <li>The Mentak player cannot place a war sun unless they have their war sun technology.<sup>4</sup>
        <ul>
        <li><b>Explicit</b>: <sup>4</sup> Designer ruling: &ldquo;Can the Mentak Coalition&rsquo;s hero, Sleeper Cell, be used to place a warsun if you do not own the warsun technology? A: No.&rdquo;</li>
        </ul></li>
    <li>The opponent may still retreat during combat.<sup>2</sup>
        <ul>
        <li><b>Explicit</b>: <sup>2</sup> RulesPal, &ldquo;How does the Mentak hero work, and can it be escaped?&rdquo;: &ldquo;The opponent can limit it by retreating.&rdquo;</li>
        </ul></li>
    </ol>

<h2 id="moll-terminus"><a href="https://twilight-imperium.fandom.com/wiki/The_Mentak_Coalition#Mech:~:text=Moll%20Terminus">Moll Terminus</a> <sub>(Mech)</sub></h2>
    <ol class="note">
    <li>If a player commits a mech to a planet that contains both a Moll Terminus mech and a PDS belonging to the Mentak player, then the committed mech cannot use its <a href="/R_sustain_damage"><sc>Sustain Damage</sc></a> ability to cancel any <a href="/R_space_cannon"><sc>Space Cannon</sc></a> hits during that invasion.<sup>*</sup>
        <ul>
        <li><b>Unverified</b>: No source found.</li>
        </ul></li>
    </ol>

